---
{
  title: "async_call_back"
}
---
### NAME

    async_call_back() - Executes a previously assembled callback, delivering
    its result through a promise.

### SYNOPSIS

    async mixed async_call_back( mixed *cb, mixed new_arg... );

### DESCRIPTION

    Executes a previously assembled callback, delivering its result through
    a promise.

    The async-aware counterpart to call_back(). Where call_back() reports
    only whether the callback errored, this delivers what it actually
    returned, and waits for it: if the callback is an async function, the
    promise adopts its promise and settles only once the callback has
    genuinely finished. An error in the callback, or a malformed callback
    structure, rejects instead.

    Await it inside an async function, or attach promise_then() outside one.
    A rejection that is never observed is reported to the debug log, so do
    not call this and discard the result.

### PARAMETERS

    cb       (mixed*)
             Callback array from assemble_call_back()

    new_arg  (...mixed)
             Additional arguments to prepend

### RETURN VALUES

    (mixed) A promise for the callback's return value, or for undefined if
    cb does not describe a callable.

### ERRORS

    If the callback structure is invalid, or the callback itself errors;
    either rejects the returned promise.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}mixed *cb = assemble_call_back(ob, "fetch_record", "gesslar");
    mapping record = await async_call_back(cb);{{di0}}
